# The held-out set's call identifiers, declared here because nothing in this
# repository can discover them.
#
# The transcripts live in `voice-agent-eval-harness-holdout` and must never be
# read from here. Identifiers are metadata, not content -- the line this project
# draws is content versus existence -- so a list of ids is safe to hold and a
# transcript is not.
#
# This mirrors `corpus/DESIGN_SET`, which declares the other half of one shared
# numbering space. Neither set is a contiguous range and neither can be inferred
# from the other: CALL-18 through CALL-20 are design calls that sit between the
# held-out ones.
#
# **Nothing here verifies this file.** It is a manual mirror of another
# repository, in the same category as everything `HOLDOUT-OBLIGATIONS.md`
# tracks, and it goes stale the same way: silently, when that repository grows.
# It replaced a hardcoded `range(13, 18)` inside `tools/statement_inventory.py`
# on 2026-09-06, after CALL-21 was added and three documents had to be corrected
# for having enumerated a set that had grown. A named file does not stop that
# happening again; it makes the place to look obvious when it does.

